module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- inhabit — the constructive dual of comprehend: SetExpr → Maybe witness.
-- decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage B (brief:
-- `workstreams/decide-substrate/briefs/phase-1-stage-B-execution.md`;
-- design: `design/deciding.md` §3 — "solve = inhabit ∘ comprehend").
--
-- Replaces BOTH v1 faces in one judgment:
--   • `witnessOfSet` (solve.fenel, WitSet marker → Maybe witness) — the Ws
--     marker vocabulary is RETIRED; inhabit reads the canonical registered
--     `Se*` SetExpr (`$tag`-based, Fenel-authorable) directly.
--   • the v1 `inhabit` (typeMarker Inh* → Maybe) — the type-marker detour is
--     gone; type-level inhabitation is `inhabit ∘ typeToSetExpr` (the Se*
--     output refit of typeToSetExpr rides Stage E; until then the refined
--     arm's TS marshal feeds `enumerableInhabit` the Se* set directly via
--     `setExprToTag`).
--
-- WITNESS RULES (the honest fences, byte-carried from witnessOfSet):
--   SeEnum      ⇒ first value (empty ⇒ Nothing)
--   SeInterval  ⇒ an INCLUSIVE bound (hi preferred, then lo); both-exclusive
--                 / unbounded-open ⇒ Nothing (ℝ has no canonical witness —
--                 the typed de-fence lives in enumerableSet's Enumerable path)
--   SeIntersect ⇒ fold the interval branches (tighter lo / tighter hi — the
--                 seIntervalFold below), witness the combined interval; a
--                 non-interval branch ⇒ Nothing (the v1 intervals-only fence)
--   SeUnion     ⇒ the first child with a Just witness
--   SeAll / SeNone / SeDiff / SeComplement / SePattern / SeWhere
--               ⇒ Nothing (documented fences — SeAll has no canonical pick,
--                 SeNone is empty, the rest are out-of-fragment v1; the
--                 Phase-4 search arc widens ∪/¬ through these honestly)
--   SeRef       ⇒ DE-FENCED at signature-substrate slice 3jw: the ten
--                 definitionally-inhabited names of `seNamedEmpty` witness to
--                 their canonical inhabitant (0 / "" / 'a' / False), each one
--                 re-checked through the `namedMember` membership seam; every
--                 other handle stays Nothing (see seWitnessRef below)
--
-- BOUND SHAPE — the live wire: `SeInterval { interval = { lo, hi } }` where
-- lo/hi are `Maybe { value, inclusive }` with BARE scalar values (exactly
-- what comprehend emits and setExprToTag preserves; the registered
-- SetBoundValue Bv* wrapping is the deciders' internal marshalled form, not
-- the wire). The WITNESS math (witInterval / witIntervalLo) is
-- representation-neutral over that Maybe-bound shape and lives HERE (moved from
-- solve.fenel with the Ws world's deletion); enumerate.fenel and refine.fenel
-- reuse it cross-file through the `module engine where` union, as does the
-- shared `seIntervalFold`.
--
-- THE INTERVAL TIGHTEN — decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage C (P-2, ONE interval
-- theory): tighterLo / tighterHi no longer carry their own raw comparison; they
-- classify the wire bounds up to the tagged `Bound` ADT and delegate to the
-- deciders' SHARED setAlgebraIntersectStepLo / -Hi (generalized to strings), so
-- there is a SINGLE interval-tighten arithmetic across the solver fold and the
-- n-ary intersectIntervals.
--
-- THE FAMILY FACE: `set:witness` (DecidableMembership's widened method)
-- adapts onto this via `setExprToTag ∘ dispatch engine:inhabit` — ONE
-- judgment core, two entries (the engine fnId + the typeclass method).
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- decide-substrate Phase 3 (the theory-family completion tail) — THE PER-SHAPE
-- WITNESS FACES. Each DecidableMembership instance now names its OWN witness
-- procedure (`seWitnessEnum` / `seWitnessInterval` / `seWitnessIntersect` /
-- `seWitnessUnion` / `seWitnessNone`; instances.fenel), and `inhabit` is the
-- THIN dispatcher over the family — it routes by the shape `$tag` (via `seTag`,
-- the propagate.fenel string discriminator) to the shape's own face, the
-- per-shape arms EXTRACTED from the old fat `case` cascade. The polymorphic
-- `set:witness` (DecidableMembership's widened method's face) stays the dispatch
-- entry (the class-method side); `inhabit` is the engine-fnId side — both
-- converge on the SAME per-shape faces. Location NOTE (a flagged brief
-- divergence): the faces live HERE in the engine module WITH the inhabit /
-- interval machinery they call (witInterval / seIntervalFold / seWitUnion —
-- same-module, no cross-module bare-name coupling), so the instances name
-- `engine:` fnIds (exactly as the Prover instance names `prover:structuralPropose`
-- and Compilable names `compile-js:*`), NOT the brief's guessed `set:*` mints.
-- The no-witness shapes share the ONE honest `seWitnessNone` face (a theory
-- with no canonical witness synthesis) — FEWER honest faces over forced-inert
-- ones. That set was 7 (All / None / Named / Pattern / Where / Diff /
-- Complement) at Phase 3; Diff left it at Phase 4 Step B (seWitnessDiff), and
-- **Named leaves it at signature-substrate slice 3jw** (seWitnessRef), so the
-- live `seWitnessNone` targets are All / None / Pattern / Where / Complement
-- and the slice-3a Rigid — SIX, and the slice must not disturb any of them.
--
-- NO ENTITY DECLS (the law-freeze rule): functions only. `WitnessVerdict` (the
-- internal three-case adjudication result the 3jw faces return) is therefore
-- declared in set-algebra-deciders.fenel, beside `seNamedEmpty` whose dual it
-- serves — same `module engine`, so the bare names resolve here.
-- =========================================================================

@label "Inhabit"
@description "The constructive dual of comprehend: extract a witness inhabitant from a canonical `Se*` SetExpr ⇒ Maybe a. The THIN dispatcher over the DecidableMembership family (decide-substrate Phase 3) — routes by the shape `$tag` (seTag) to each theory's OWN per-shape witness face: SeEnum ⇒ seWitnessEnum (first value); SeInterval ⇒ seWitnessInterval (an INCLUSIVE bound — hi preferred, then lo; both-exclusive / unbounded-open ⇒ Nothing, the ℝ honesty fence); SeIntersect ⇒ seWitnessIntersect (fold the interval branches, witness the combined interval; a non-interval branch ⇒ Nothing, v1); SeUnion ⇒ seWitnessUnion (the first child's Just); everything else ⇒ seWitnessFallback, which routes SeRef to seWitnessRef (signature-substrate slice 3jw — the ten definitionally-inhabited names witness to their canonical inhabitant, membership-re-checked) and delegates the rest to seWitnessNone (Nothing — the remaining documented no-witness fences: SeAll has no canonical pick, SeNone is empty, SeComplement / SePattern / SeWhere are out-of-fragment v1, SeRigid is the validation-only rigid atom). `solve = inhabit ∘ comprehend` LITERALLY; the DecidableMembership `witness` method dispatches to the SAME per-shape faces. Replaces witnessOfSet (Ws markers) + the Inh* type-marker inhabit. decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage B; per-shape faces Phase 3."
@tags "engine" "solve" "inhabit" "prover" "decide-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-3"
-- signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — NO WITNESS AT A RIGID. `SeRigid`
-- rides the trailing fall-through to Nothing, and that is the DECIDED answer,
-- not an oversight: a witness would be a ground value claimed to inhabit κ, and
-- no ground value survives the κ := ∅ instantiation.
--
-- It is documented here instead of written as a ninth `else if` arm because
-- this declaration is at 119 of the parser's 120-token per-decl budget
-- (PVF_DECL_CAP); one more arm pushes it to 132 and would force
-- inhabit.fenel into FENCE_FALLBACK, i.e. spend a real parser fence on an arm
-- whose behaviour is identical to the fall-through it replaces. The
-- exhaustiveness meta-test reads this documented fence for `inhabit`.
--
-- signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — the fall-through is now `seWitnessFallback`
-- rather than `seWitnessNone` directly. This is a SWAP OF ONE IDENTIFIER FOR
-- ANOTHER, measured token-NEUTRAL (119 → 119), so the budget note above still
-- holds exactly. `seWitnessFallback` routes ONLY `SeRef` to the new
-- `seWitnessRef` face and delegates all six other tail shapes — SeAll, SeNone,
-- SePattern, SeWhere, SeComplement and SeRigid, including the rigid fence
-- documented immediately above — to `seWitnessNone` unchanged.
inhabit : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
inhabit s =
  let t = seTag s
  if eq t "SeEnum" then seWitnessEnum s
  else if eq t "SeInterval" then seWitnessInterval s
  else if eq t "SeIntersect" then seWitnessIntersect s
  else if eq t "SeUnion" then seWitnessUnion s
  else if eq t "SeDiff" then seWitnessDiff s
  else if eq t "SeCtor" then seWitnessCtor s
  else if eq t "SeMu" then seWitnessMu s
  else if eq t "SeArrow" then seWitnessArrow s
  else seWitnessFallback s

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The per-shape witness faces — the DecidableMembership instances' `witness`
-- method targets (decide-substrate Phase 3). Each takes the WHOLE SetExpr (the
-- family contract `witness : SetExpr -> Maybe a`) and re-matches its own shape
-- (returning Nothing on a mismatch — a standalone, individually-dispatchable
-- per-shape procedure). The pattern style is inhabit's proven-non-fenced form.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "inhabit: seWitnessEnum"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 3 — the SeEnum theory's witness face: the first enum value (empty ⇒ Nothing). The DecidableMembership SetEnum instance's `witness` method target; inhabit dispatches here for enum shapes. Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessEnum : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe Any
seWitnessEnum s =
  case s of
    SeEnum { values = vs } -> head vs
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: seWitnessInterval"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 3 — the SeInterval theory's witness face: an INCLUSIVE bound (hi preferred, then lo; both-exclusive / unbounded-open ⇒ Nothing — the ℝ honesty fence). The DecidableMembership SetInterval instance's `witness` method target. Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessInterval : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe Any
seWitnessInterval s =
  case s of
    SeInterval { interval = iv } -> witInterval iv.lo iv.hi
    _ -> Nothing

-- decide-substrate Phase 4 Step B — the composite witness faces WIDEN onto the
-- search core. The DECIDABLE FAST-PATH runs FIRST (byte-preserving every
-- today-Just — the differential's HARD rule: no Just→Just change), then on
-- Nothing the fuel-bounded `searchDefault` (search.fenel) widens the fenced tail
-- (enum∩enum, generator+¬filter, the mixed intersects the interval-fold
-- fences, deeper unions). NOTE — this REFINES the brief's "delete the fast-path
-- arms, route purely through search": search does NOT byte-preserve the
-- fast-path's endpoint choice (witInterval prefers the hi endpoint; the search
-- generator tries the lo endpoint first) nor the union first-child order for
-- unions of search-witnessable composites, so a PURE replacement would change
-- pinned witnesses (a Just→Just violation). Fast-path-first + search-on-Nothing
-- is the conservative extension: every gain is a strictly-better Nothing→Just.
-- The fast-path arms (seWitIntersect / seWitUnion / seIntervalFold / witInterval)
-- STAY — they are ALSO the shared interval math enumerate.fenel / refine.fenel
-- reuse cross-file, and search itself reuses seIntervalFold via seCandidates.

@label "inhabit: seWitnessIntersect"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 3 / Phase 4 Step B — the SeIntersect theory's witness face: the interval-fold FAST PATH first (seWitIntersect — fold the interval branches into one combined interval, tighter lo / tighter hi, then witness it; byte-preserved), and on Nothing the fuel-bounded search widens (enum∩enum, generator+¬filter, mixed intersects). The DecidableMembership SetIntersect instance's `witness` method target. Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "search" "decide-substrate" "phase-3" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessIntersect : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessIntersect s =
  case s of
    SeIntersect { branches = bs } ->
      case seWitIntersect bs of
        Just w -> Just w
        Nothing -> svToMaybe (searchDefault s)
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: seWitnessUnion"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 3 / Phase 4 Step B — the SeUnion theory's witness face: the first-child FAST PATH first (seWitUnion — the first child whose inhabit is Just; byte-preserved order + value), and on Nothing the fuel-bounded search widens (a union whose every child needs composite search — empty-branch pruned). The DecidableMembership SetUnion instance's `witness` method target. Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "search" "decide-substrate" "phase-3" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessUnion : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessUnion s =
  case s of
    SeUnion { branches = bs } ->
      case seWitUnion bs of
        Just w -> Just w
        Nothing -> svToMaybe (searchDefault s)
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: seWitnessDiff"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 4 Step B — the SeDiff theory's witness face (NEW — search-backed): `a \\ b` witnesses via the search core as `a ∩ ¬b` (a generator from `a`, the negative filter `¬b`). The old SetDiff instance pointed `witness` at seWitnessNone (always Nothing); this is a pure Nothing→Just widening (the old fence had no decidable fast path). The DecidableMembership SetDiff instance's `witness` method target. Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "search" "decide-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessDiff : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessDiff s = svToMaybe (searchDefault s)

@label "inhabit: seWitnessNone"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 3 — the SHARED no-witness face: the theories with no canonical witness synthesis all dispatch their `witness` here ⇒ Nothing. One honest face over several forced-inert ones (the brief's fewer-honest-faces rule). The live set is SIX — SetAll (no canonical pick), SetNone (empty), SetPattern / SetWhere / SetComplement (out-of-fragment v1) and SetRigid (a ground witness would not survive κ := ∅). It was seven at Phase 3; SetDiff left at Phase 4 Step B (seWitnessDiff) and SetNamed at signature-substrate slice 3jw (seWitnessRef). Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessNone : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessNone s = Nothing

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — THE WITNESS DE-FENCE for `SeRef`.
--
-- WHY THIS IS NOT A NEW TRUSTED INFERENCE. The shape is PROPOSE → RE-CHECK →
-- ADJUDICATE. `seNamedWitnessPick` (set-algebra-deciders.fenel) proposes a
-- canonical inhabitant from a ten-name table; the proposal is HEURISTIC and
-- UNTRUSTED. It is then re-checked through `namedMember` — the ledgered
-- `mem.ref` THEORY-PLUGIN seam — and only a `Just true` is accepted. The step
-- from `{w} ⊆ SeRef h` to `JInhabited (SeRef h)` is the ledger's
-- `k.rule.witness`, an AXIOM already in the design/floor-kernel.md §3.2 basis.
-- So the cascade adds NOTHING to the TCB: a bad proposal yields `Nothing`,
-- never a false `Just`. TCB row `wit.ref`, THEOREM under that NARROW claim
-- only — not a claim about registry completeness, and not a claim that the ten
-- names are the right ten.
--
-- CONTEXT SCOPE (option (a), narrow). `inhabit` takes no account and no
-- resolver, so the theorem is stated for GLOBAL / UNRESOLVED / NO-ACCOUNT
-- semantics. The witness is NOT claimed valid under a per-request resolver or
-- an account-scoped named-set override. See `wit.ref` and the §8 queue: the
-- context-free witness surfaces (notably the editor typed-hole seam, which
-- calls `witnessOf` with no account) are recorded as global-only.
--
-- THE CONTRADICTION GUARD IS DEFENCE-IN-DEPTH, AND ITS REACHABILITY IS STATED
-- HONESTLY. All ten names answer `seNamedEmpty = Just false`, so no ordinary
-- production input can reach `mem = Just True ∧ emp = Just True`. The guard
-- exists because the two tables are INDEPENDENT and a future widening of one
-- without the other would silently produce exactly that conflict. The gate
-- therefore executes the guard through the real functions with injected
-- verdicts rather than pretending a live input reaches it.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "inhabit: seWitnessAdjudicate"
@description "signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — the three-verdict witness decision, given a proposed witness and the two independent oracle verdicts (membership of the proposal, emptiness of the set). `mem = Just True` and `emp = Just True` CONTRADICT — the set is claimed both to contain the witness and to be empty — so the answer is WContradiction, never a witness. `mem = Just True` alone ⇒ WAccept. Anything else (Just False, or the undecided Nothing) ⇒ WAbstain: the Tri discipline, where an undecided oracle is never read as agreement. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "witness" "signature-substrate" "slice-3jw"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessAdjudicate : (w: Any) -> (mem: Maybe Boolean) -> (emp: Maybe Boolean) -> WitnessVerdict
seWitnessAdjudicate w mem emp =
  case mem of
    Just True ->
      case emp of
        Just True -> WContradiction { diag = "seWitnessAdjudicate: namedMember accepts the witness while seNamedEmpty reports the set EMPTY" }
        _ -> WAccept { w = w }
    _ -> WAbstain

@label "inhabit: seWitnessRefPick"
@description "signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — the INTERNAL witness face for a named set: propose a canonical inhabitant (seNamedWitnessPick), RE-CHECK it through the namedMember membership seam, and hand both verdicts plus the emptiness verdict to seWitnessAdjudicate VERBATIM (a tail call — there is no room here to inspect, launder or override the adjudicator's result). A name outside the ten proposes nothing ⇒ WAbstain, the honest fence. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "witness" "signature-substrate" "slice-3jw"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessRefPick : (h: String) -> WitnessVerdict
seWitnessRefPick h =
  case seNamedWitnessPick h of
    Nothing -> WAbstain
    Just w -> seWitnessAdjudicate w (namedMember h w) (seNamedEmpty h)

@label "inhabit: wvToMaybe"
@description "signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — the thin public projection of the internal WitnessVerdict onto the family's `Maybe` contract: WAccept ⇒ Just its witness; WAbstain AND WContradiction both ⇒ Nothing. Projecting both refusal cases to Nothing loses nothing an existing witness consumer needs — the diagnostic belongs to the internal/audit face. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "witness" "signature-substrate" "slice-3jw"
@category "engine-internal"
wvToMaybe : (v: WitnessVerdict) -> Maybe a
wvToMaybe v =
  case v of
    WAccept { w = w } -> Just w
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: seWitnessRef"
@description "signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — the SeRef theory's witness face (NEW): the constructive dual of seNamedEmpty. A named set among the ten definitionally-inhabited names witnesses to its canonical inhabitant (0 / \"\" / 'a' / False), membership-re-checked through namedMember; every other handle — an unknown name, a registered entity name, a μ-bound var — stays fenced at Nothing. Replaces seWitnessNone as the DecidableMembership SetNamed instance's witness target. Per-shape face."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "witness" "signature-substrate" "slice-3jw"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessRef : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessRef s =
  case s of
    SeRef { handle = h } -> wvToMaybe (seWitnessRefPick h)
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: seWitnessFallback"
@description "signature-substrate slice 3jw §2 — inhabit's fall-through, one level of indirection over the old trailing `else seWitnessNone s`: a SeRef routes to the new seWitnessRef face, EVERY other shape (SeAll / SeNone / SePattern / SeWhere / SeComplement / SeRigid) delegates to seWitnessNone unchanged. Swapping one identifier for another in inhabit's dispatcher is token-NEUTRAL, so the 119-of-120 PVF_DECL_CAP budget is untouched; adding a ninth arm instead would push it to 132 and fence the file. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "witness" "signature-substrate" "slice-3jw"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessFallback : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessFallback s =
  if eq (seTag s) "SeRef" then seWitnessRef s
  else seWitnessNone s

-- seWitIntersect — fold interval branches to a combined interval, witness it.
@label "inhabit: seWitIntersect"
@description "Stage B — witness of a SeIntersect: fold the branches into one combined interval (seIntervalFold — tighter lo / tighter hi), then witInterval it. A non-interval branch marks the fold un-decidable (ok=false ⇒ Nothing — the v1 fence). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitIntersect : (bs: a) -> Maybe a
seWitIntersect bs =
  let acc = seIntervalFold bs { lo = Nothing, hi = Nothing, ok = true }
  if acc.ok then witInterval acc.lo acc.hi else Nothing

-- seWitUnion — the first child with a Just witness (inhabit recursion).
@label "inhabit: seWitUnion"
@description "Stage B — witness of a SeUnion: the first child whose inhabit is Just; Nothing when no child witnesses. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitUnion : (bs: a) -> Maybe a
seWitUnion bs =
  case head bs of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just b ->
      case inhabit b of
        Just v -> Just v
        Nothing ->
          case tail bs of
            Nothing -> Nothing
            Just rest -> seWitUnion rest

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- seIntervalFold — THE shared Se-interval combiner: fold a SetExpr branch
-- list into one `{ lo, hi, ok }` (tighter lo / tighter hi; any non-SeInterval
-- branch ⇒ ok=false). The Se* successor of the Ws-reading witIntersectFold;
-- reused by refine.fenel (refineIntersect) + enumerate.fenel (the optimize
-- tiers + the typed Enumerable steppers) cross-file.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "inhabit: seIntervalFold"
@description "Stage B — accumulator-threaded fold over SeIntersect branches, threading the running { lo, hi, ok } (tighterLo / tighterHi per SeInterval branch; a non-interval branch sets ok=false). The shared Se-interval combiner reused by inhabit / refine / enumerate. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
seIntervalFold : (branches: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
seIntervalFold branches acc =
  case head branches of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just b ->
      let acc2 = seIntervalStep acc b
      case tail branches of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> seIntervalFold rest acc2

-- seIntervalStep — tighten the running bounds by one SeInterval branch.
@label "inhabit: seIntervalStep"
@description "Stage B — tighten the running { lo, hi } by one SeInterval branch (tighterLo / tighterHi over the interval payload's Maybe-bounds); a non-interval branch sets ok=false (the intervals-only fence). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "decide-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
seIntervalStep : (acc: a) -> (b: SetExpr) -> a
seIntervalStep acc b =
  case b of
    SeInterval { interval = iv } -> { lo = tighterLo acc.lo iv.lo, hi = tighterHi acc.hi iv.hi, ok = acc.ok }
    _ -> { lo = acc.lo, hi = acc.hi, ok = false }

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The bound MATH — representation-neutral over `Maybe { value, inclusive }`
-- (moved from solve.fenel with the Ws world's deletion; P5 lineage).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- witInterval — an inclusive bound (hi preferred), else Nothing.
@label "solve: witInterval"
@description "Phase 5 — witness of an interval: the hi bound when inclusive, else the lo bound when inclusive, else Nothing (both-exclusive / unbounded-open — the ℝ honesty fence). Representation-neutral over Maybe { value, inclusive } bounds. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "expr-substrate" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
witInterval : (lo: a) -> (hi: a) -> Maybe a
witInterval lo hi =
  case hi of
    Just b -> if b.inclusive then Just b.value else witIntervalLo lo
    Nothing -> witIntervalLo lo

-- witIntervalLo — the lo bound when inclusive, else Nothing.
@label "solve: witIntervalLo"
@description "Phase 5 — witInterval fallthrough: the lo bound when inclusive, else Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "expr-substrate" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
witIntervalLo : (lo: a) -> Maybe a
witIntervalLo lo =
  case lo of
    Just b -> if b.inclusive then Just b.value else Nothing
    Nothing -> Nothing

-- tighterLo / tighterHi — the more restrictive interval bound (larger lo /
-- smaller hi, exclusive-on-tie). decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage C (the P-2
-- merge — ONE interval theory): the raw-bound comparison is GONE; the solver
-- fold now shares the deciders' Bound-ADT tighten (setAlgebraIntersectStepLo /
-- -Hi, generalized to strings) by classifying its raw `{value, inclusive}`
-- Maybe-bounds up to the tagged `Bound` ADT (setAlgebraClassifyMaybeBound),
-- tightening there, and declassifying back down (setAlgebraDeclassifyMaybeBound)
-- — so there is a SINGLE interval-tighten arithmetic across the solver fold and
-- the deciders' n-ary intersectIntervals. Byte-identical to the pre-merge
-- number-only form (verified across every inclusive tie-break combo); strings
-- now tighten (they did in the pre-merge solver form too — pure carry).
@label "solve: tighterLo"
@description "Phase 5 / decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage C — the more restrictive lower bound (larger value, exclusive-on-tie; unbounded loses). Classifies the raw Maybe-bounds to the tagged Bound ADT and delegates to the SHARED setAlgebraIntersectStepLo (the ONE interval tighten), then declassifies. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "expr-substrate" "phase-5" "decide-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
tighterLo : (a: a) -> (b: a) -> a
tighterLo a b =
  setAlgebraDeclassifyMaybeBound (setAlgebraIntersectStepLo (setAlgebraClassifyMaybeBound a) (setAlgebraClassifyMaybeBound b))

-- tighterHi — the more restrictive (smaller-valued, exclusive-on-tie) hi bound.
@label "solve: tighterHi"
@description "Phase 5 / decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage C — the more restrictive upper bound (smaller value, exclusive-on-tie; unbounded loses). Classifies the raw Maybe-bounds to the tagged Bound ADT and delegates to the SHARED setAlgebraIntersectStepHi (the ONE interval tighten), then declassifies. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "expr-substrate" "phase-5" "decide-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
tighterHi : (a: a) -> (b: a) -> a
tighterHi a b =
  setAlgebraDeclassifyMaybeBound (setAlgebraIntersectStepHi (setAlgebraClassifyMaybeBound a) (setAlgebraClassifyMaybeBound b))

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1b — the SeCtor + SeMu witness faces.
--
-- seWitnessCtor: a constructor set's canonical witness is the value built
-- from each field's witness — `{$tag: c, f1: w1, …}` (the pure-ADT view; a
-- synthetic record ctor "" gets no $tag). The value is assembled via the
-- `mapSet` dynamic-key native (the decl-grammar `mapSet {} "repr" …`
-- precedent) because a `.fenel` record literal cannot author a `$`-prefixed
-- KEY — the string "$tag" as an ARGUMENT is plain data (the dtLitTag
-- read-side precedent). Coercing ctors (True/False) ⇒ Nothing (the ledger-B5
-- exclusion — their construct coerces to a native rep, so the tagged record
-- would be a lie).
--
-- seWitnessMu: μ-inhabitation = fuel-bounded KLEENE iteration (design
-- §0.3): try inhabit(F(∅)), then inhabit(F²(∅)), … — each iterate is an
-- ordinary SetExpr this dispatcher already handles (the SeCtor face makes
-- ADT iterates witnessable). The rung's "depth/fuel discipline" bounds BOTH
-- axes: iterate COUNT (fixed 8 — no caller dial, the D′ fixed-fuel
-- precedent) and iterate SIZE (seSize > 512 ⇒ Nothing — substitution can
-- duplicate the body per occurrence). Soundness (Fⁿ(∅) ⊆ LFP) needs F
-- monotone ⇒ gated on positive ∧ supported. `inhabit ⟦List a⟧` ⇒
-- `{$tag:"Nil"}` at the first iterate.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "inhabit: seWitnessCtor"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1b — the SeCtor theory's witness face: build the canonical inhabitant `{$tag: c, field: witness(set), …}` from each field's own inhabit witness (any field Nothing ⇒ Nothing; a nullary ctor ⇒ just the tag record; the synthetic record ctor \"\" ⇒ no $tag). Assembled via the mapSet dynamic-key native (a record literal cannot author a $-prefixed key; the string \"$tag\" as an argument is data — the dtLitTag read-side precedent). Coercing ctors (True/False) ⇒ Nothing (ledger-B5). Per-shape face; inhabit dispatches here for SeCtor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "sector" "decide-substrate" "phase-8mu"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessCtor : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessCtor s =
  case s of
    SeCtor { ctor = c, fields = fs } ->
      if not (fieldSemanticSlotsValid fs) then Nothing
      else if seCtorCoercing c then Nothing
      else
        let base = if eq c "" then {} else mapSet {} "$tag" c
        swcFields fs base
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: swcFields"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1b — the seWitnessCtor field fold: witness each field's set via inhabit and mapSet it onto the accumulating record; any Nothing ⇒ Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "sector" "decide-substrate" "phase-8mu"
@category "engine-internal"
swcFields : (fs: List SetCtorField) -> (acc: {}) -> Maybe ({})
swcFields fs acc = case head fs of
  Nothing -> Just acc
  Just f ->
    case inhabit f.set of
      Nothing -> Nothing
      Just w -> swcFields (eufRest fs) (mapSet acc f.wireName w)

@label "inhabit: seWitnessMu"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1b — the SeMu theory's witness face: fuel-bounded Kleene iteration `inhabit(Fⁿ(∅))` (design/mu-induction.md §0.3) — S₀=∅, Sᵢ₊₁=substSet v Sᵢ F, first Just wins; fixed fuel 8 iterations + a seSize>512 iterate-size guard (the depth/fuel discipline bounds both axes). Gated on positive ∧ supported (Fⁿ(∅) ⊆ LFP needs monotone F). `inhabit ⟦List a⟧ = Just {$tag:\"Nil\"}` at the first iterate. Per-shape face; inhabit dispatches here for SeMu."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "mu" "decide-substrate" "phase-8mu"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessMu : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe a
seWitnessMu s =
  case s of
    SeMu { var = v, body = f } ->
      if seMuFaceOk v f
      then
        let bot = SeNone
        swmKleene v f bot 8
      else Nothing
    _ -> Nothing

@label "inhabit: swmKleene"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1b — the Kleene loop of seWitnessMu: next = substSet v cur F; size-guard (seSize > 512 ⇒ Nothing); inhabit next — Just w ⇒ Just w, Nothing ⇒ recurse with next and fuel−1; fuel exhausted ⇒ Nothing (never a false accept). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "mu" "decide-substrate" "phase-8mu"
@category "engine-internal"
swmKleene : (v: String) -> (f: a) -> (cur: a) -> (fuel: Number) -> Maybe b
swmKleene v f cur fuel =
  if lte fuel 0 then Nothing
  else
    let next = substSet v cur f
    if gt (seSize next) 512 then Nothing
    else
      case inhabit next of
        Just w -> Just w
        Nothing -> swmKleene v f next (sub fuel 1)

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- decide-substrate Phase 8λ.1 — the SeArrow witness face (the exponential
-- inhabitation floor, design/arrow-synthesis.md §0.1): the two cheap
-- witnesses. Some param decidably EMPTY ⇒ a VACUOUS lambda (never called ⇒ any
-- body); else inhabit(returns) = Just w ⇒ the CONST lambda `\_ -> w`
-- (arity-matched). The witness value is a closure of the right arity
-- (`{__fenelFn, params, body, closure}` — json-logic.ts:isClosure) so the value
-- taxonomy is the Ref substrate's, not a new one.
--
-- HONESTY (the 8λ.1 GAP — CLOSED at 8λ.2): the returned closure's own kernel
-- re-certification (`{closure} ⊆ SeArrow`) now DECIDES (the CHECK face type-checks
-- a lambda).
--
-- THE 8λ.6 CORRECTION — "fast-path-first, byte-preserving every today-Just" was
-- the headline here and it is now FALSE, deliberately. The const-first probe was
-- the FIRST of six point-pre-emption surfaces, and while it stood it masked the
-- other five: once `inhabit` gained cheap points for the named sets, every arrow
-- collapsed to `\_ -> <point>` and goal-directed synthesis degraded from
-- informative terms to constants. The adapter therefore keeps NO vacuity branch
-- and NO const branch: every valid SeArrow goal routes through
-- `synthesizeArrow`'s PREFERENCE-ORDERED candidate search, which offers the
-- root-spine vacuous candidate first, then the admitted batch sorted by
-- `(base-free before point-dependent, var < ctor < apply < case, source
-- ordinal, admission rank)`, then ONE uncharged bare point reserve. A constant
-- is still reachable — it is simply no longer preferred over an admitted
-- base-free term. Headline, restored: `inhabit ⟦(Int)→Int⟧` is `Just (\x -> x)`
-- because the identity is base-free and `\_ -> 0` is not.
--
-- What replaced the retired byte-preservation claim is narrower and true: at a
-- FIXED fuel and admission budget, with unchanged existing point values and only
-- a `Nothing -> Just` point extension, the previously returned admitted
-- base-free winner is unchanged. When fuel or budget GROWS the guarantee is
-- `Found -> Found`, not witness-byte stability.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "inhabit: seWitnessArrow"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8λ.1 / 8λ.3 / 8λ.6 — the SeArrow theory's witness face. Valid semantic slots ⇒ the whole goal goes to `synthesizeArrow`'s preference-ordered candidate search; there is no const-first or vacuity-first probe left here, because either one masked the ordering fixes by returning a constant before the search ran. The search itself owns root vacuity (offered first, at every fuel and budget), the admitted batch sorted base-free before point-dependent, and the ONE uncharged bare point reserve offered last. The witness is a closure `{__fenelFn, params, body, closure}` (the Ref substrate's callable rep) whose own kernel re-certification DECIDES (the 8λ.2 CHECK face; every returned TvFound is self-re-checked BY CONSTRUCTION, so it is kernel-CERTIFIABLE — not necessarily kernel-certified, since this face does not itself take the kernel round-trip). Per-shape face; inhabit dispatches here for SeArrow."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "arrow" "synthesize" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessArrow : (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe Any
seWitnessArrow s =
  case s of
    SeArrow { params = ps, returns = r } ->
      if fieldSemanticSlotsValid ps then seWitnessArrowGo ps r s else Nothing
    _ -> Nothing

-- seWitnessArrowGo — the SeArrow witness dispatch. It USED to hold a 3-way if
-- (vacuous first; then an ARROW-returning goal straight through synthesis's
-- intro; else the ground const with synthesis on the Nothing tail). All three
-- branches are GONE at 8λ.6: each was a point-pre-emption surface, and the const
-- branch masked the other five by returning `\_ -> inhabit(returns)` before any
-- ordering could be observed. What survives is the REASON the arrow-return
-- branch existed — a const-of-closure body embeds a CLOSURE VALUE as `body`,
-- which bodyToExpr cannot lift back to an Expr, so the witness would fail its
-- own re-certification (the probe-caught nested-closure gap). The ordered search
-- preserves that structurally rather than by branching: a Point never forms at
-- an arrow subgoal, and no path embeds a closure in an `ELit`.
@label "inhabit: seWitnessArrowGo"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8λ.1 / 8λ.3 / 8λ.6 — the SeArrow witness dispatch. After slot validation it keeps NO vacuity branch and NO arrow-return branch: EVERY valid SeArrow goal routes through the ordered candidate search, which owns root vacuity, the admitted window and the one bare reserve. Leaving either fast path here would mask every preference fix behind a constant. Internal helper to seWitnessArrow."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "arrow" "synthesize" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessArrowGo : (ps: List SetArrowParam) -> (r: SetExpr) -> (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe Any
seWitnessArrowGo ps r s = seWitnessArrowConst (map (\p -> p.wireName) ps) r s

@label "inhabit: seWitnessArrowConst"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8λ.6 — the arity-3 thin delegate. Its const-first `inhabit returns` probe is DELETED: the whole arrow goal goes to `synthesizeArrow`, whose ordered search offers the root vacuous candidate first, then the preference-sorted admitted batch, then the one uncharged bare point reserve — so a constant is still reachable, but only after every admitted base-free candidate. Projected via tvToMaybe. Internal helper to seWitnessArrowGo."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "arrow" "synthesize" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
seWitnessArrowConst : (pnames: List String) -> (r: SetExpr) -> (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe Any
seWitnessArrowConst pnames r s = tvToMaybe (synthesizeArrow 8 s)

@label "inhabit: mkArrowClosure"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8λ.1 — build the const/vacuous-witness closure `{__fenelFn: true, params, body, closure: {}}` (the Ref substrate's isClosure shape). Assembled via the mapSet dynamic-key native rather than a record literal: a `{__fenelFn: true, …}` LITERAL is the evaluator's closure SENTINEL — it would leave `params`/`body` as UNEVALUATED JSON-Logic (`{var:\"pnames\"}`), so the fields are set as DATA via mapSet (the seWitnessCtor $tag-authoring precedent). Internal helper to seWitnessArrow."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "arrow" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
mkArrowClosure : (pnames: List String) -> (body: Any) -> {}
mkArrowClosure pnames body =
  let r0 = mapSet {} "__fenelFn" true
  let r1 = mapSet r0 "params" pnames
  let r2 = mapSet r1 "body" body
  mapSet r2 "closure" {}

@label "inhabit: arrowSomeParamEmpty"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 8λ.1 — does SOME SeArrow param have a decidably-EMPTY domain (⇒ the vacuous-function witness inhabits — the param is never supplied)? Any Just true ⇒ true; else false. Internal helper to seWitnessArrow."
@tags "engine" "internal" "solve" "inhabit" "arrow" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
arrowSomeParamEmpty : (ps: List SetArrowParam) -> Boolean
arrowSomeParamEmpty ps = case head ps of
  Nothing -> false
  Just p ->
    case setAlgebraDecideEmpty p.set of
      Just true -> true
      _ -> arrowSomeParamEmpty (eufRest ps)
